pr_body:
Removes the SVGO transformer (by moving SVGO into the react-svg transformer) and adds a SVGO optimizer

Closes T-1080
Closes https://github.com/parcel-bundler/parcel/issues/6365

One problem with svgo 2 is that it's really designed for JS config files. The way to disable only one plugin and keep the rest at the default setting is
```js
// svgo.config.js
const { extendDefaultPlugins } = require('svgo');
module.exports = {
  plugins: extendDefaultPlugins([
    {
      name: 'builtinPluginName',
      active: false
    }
  ])
}
```
https://github.com/svg/svgo#configuration

https://github.com/svg/svgo/issues/1497

Not entirely sure if SVGO in the react-svg transformer should only be enabled if `shouldOptimize`, because svg files from editors can be massive

